1. Ownership
The source code, design, text, database structure, SQL, graphics layout,
file formats and every other part of this software (the "Work") were created
by Mohamed Aziz Ladhari (the "Author") and remain his exclusive property.
Nothing in this repository, in the running app, or in any use of either
transfers ownership or any right to anyone. Showing the Work to a school,
a teacher, an administrator or a reviewer is not a transfer, a sale, a
donation or an assignment. The Author keeps the right to be named as the
Author of the Work in every place it is used, shown or described.

2. What you may do
You may open the running app and use it if the Author or the Primum Auxilium
team has given you an account. You may read the files in this repository
only to check their security or to learn how the app behaves, and only for
as long as the Author allows it. Nothing else is allowed.

3. What you may not do without the Author's written permission
(a) copy, download, clone, fork, mirror, archive, scrape or store the Work
    or any part of it, except the temporary copy a browser makes to show it;
(b) run, host, deploy, resell, rent, lend, sublicense or publish the Work or
    anything built from it;
(c) modify, translate, adapt, rebrand, rename, re-skin or build a derivative
    or similar work from it;
(d) remove, hide or change any author name, notice, marker or watermark;
(e) claim, state or suggest that you or anyone other than the Author wrote,
    designed or owns the Work;
(f) reverse engineer, decompile, deobfuscate, probe or test the app, its
    servers or its database without the Author's written permission;
(g) bypass or try to bypass any access control, sign-in, role or protection;
(h) use the Work, its text or its code to train, tune or evaluate any
    machine learning or artificial intelligence system;
(i) request, demand or take the Author's database, SQL files, keys, passwords
    or back-ups as a condition of anything. Those are private to the Author.

4. Personal data
Student records, identity documents and photos handled by the app are
personal data. They may be viewed only by the people the app's privacy policy
names and only for the purpose stated there. Copying or passing them on is
forbidden and may be a violation of the Kingdom's Personal Data Protection
Law.

5. Permission and the school
The Author may grant permission in writing, signed and dated by him. A
permission is limited to what it says, can be withdrawn by him, and never
gives ownership. Use of the app by Middle East International School - Al
Wurud or its students while the Author is a member of the team does not
give the school any right over the source code beyond section 2.

6. Protection under Saudi law
This Work is protected by the Saudi Copyright Law (Royal Decree No. M/41
dated 2/7/1441H) and its regulations, and the Author's rights include the
right of attribution and the right to object to any change or use that harms
his name or the Work. Unauthorised access, copying or interference may also
be an offence under the Anti-Cyber Crime Law (Royal Decree No. M/17 dated
8/3/1428H). The Author may seek every remedy these laws give him, including
orders to stop use, removal, damages and referral to the competent
authority.

7. Breach
Any breach ends all permission at once without notice. You must stop using
the Work and delete every copy you hold.

8. No warranty
The Work is provided as it is, without any warranty. The Author is not
liable for any loss arising from its use.

9. Governing law
This license is governed by the laws of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. Any
